<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bicc Cafca half yr shr dives into loss.</title>
<headline>Bicc Cafca half yr shr dives into loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended June 30.</p>
<p>			(million Z$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1 loss	vs    31 profit</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs    21</p>
<p>Retained earnings for</p>
<p>    the period		0.4 loss    vs    3.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.4 loss    vs    16.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 nil	   vs    6.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		  96.9	  vs  118.8</p>
<p>Full name: Bicc Cafca Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company does not hold sanguine expectations for the next six months and the outlook is a break-even position for the full year, before finance charges.</p>
<p>Factors which may impact positively on the forecast are lower copper prices, the lower bank rates recently announced, a successful outcome to tariff reforms and growth in those sectors which have a requirement for cable.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
